		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:7vkbgl7un45tvxva25j24yyu/app.bsky.feed.post/3larfdwr2fk2n",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3larf5rq7jc2o",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/polyglotprog.bsky.social/post/3larfdwr2fk2n",
			"author": {
				"name": "PolyglotProg",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/polyglotprog.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:7vkbgl7un45tvxva25j24yyu/bafkreibzdmdtsygkwyd2wkhrcsyowgfl4igmvoy7cpsdag5aelas44mdwu"
			},
			"date": "2024-11-12T17:48:39.366Z",
			"content": "<p>You are excused.. but yes an SVG is not an image file per se.. its an XML instruction set. Which makes it different that other rasterized images, as well as different from other vector based image formats. SVG is a format that describes the image it wants to make, it isn't the image itself.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:c577wa5hifxtmprlqc5mo5cb/app.bsky.feed.post/3larfkxmaik26",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3larf6hbbd22o",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/ericwbailey.website/post/3larfkxmaik26",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eric Bailey",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/ericwbailey.website",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:c577wa5hifxtmprlqc5mo5cb/bafkreihpor2oxmufrmbnapr3n4vp6zopr4bvlwciiaholzd7dxe3tpzopi"
			},
