			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:n5llt2bsouzutg6xf6jg7u34/app.bsky.feed.post/3largfo5zwc2x",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:7vkbgl7un45tvxva25j24yyu/app.bsky.feed.post/3larfdwr2fk2n",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/jeffchausse.bsky.social/post/3largfo5zwc2x",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jeff Chausse",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/jeffchausse.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:n5llt2bsouzutg6xf6jg7u34/bafkreifk2b3fp3oppec7jduqdsbafj4ualmxlw4mpddgvfz36txos74ixq"
			},
			"date": "2024-11-12T18:07:31.205Z",
			"content": "<p>Isn’t every image file a description of how to make an image?</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3larguyut6k26",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:n5llt2bsouzutg6xf6jg7u34/app.bsky.feed.post/3largfo5zwc2x",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3larguyut6k26",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2024-11-12T18:16:05.754Z",
			"content": "<p>before we go down that road (and for the record), Preview isn’t limited to “image files”</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:7vkbgl7un45tvxva25j24yyu/app.bsky.feed.post/3largvwekfk2n",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:n5llt2bsouzutg6xf6jg7u34/app.bsky.feed.post/3largfo5zwc2x",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/polyglotprog.bsky.social/post/3largvwekfk2n",
			"author": {
				"name": "PolyglotProg",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/polyglotprog.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:7vkbgl7un45tvxva25j24yyu/bafkreibzdmdtsygkwyd2wkhrcsyowgfl4igmvoy7cpsdag5aelas44mdwu"
			},
			"date": "2024-11-12T18:16:36.679Z",
			"content": "<p>Nope.. bitmap images contain both the canvas in the form of a resolution, as well as the individual pixel data. The computer that is rendering it has to make no determination as to how to do that, as it isn't an instruction, its a self-contained image.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:7vkbgl7un45tvxva25j24yyu/app.bsky.feed.post/3largzvg33c2n",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3larguyut6k26",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/polyglotprog.bsky.social/post/3largzvg33c2n",
			"author": {
				"name": "PolyglotProg",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/polyglotprog.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:7vkbgl7un45tvxva25j24yyu/bafkreibzdmdtsygkwyd2wkhrcsyowgfl4igmvoy7cpsdag5aelas44mdwu"
			},
			"date": "2024-11-12T18:18:49.897Z",
			"content": "<p>No... that is absolutely correct. But given that preview works as a rasterized display window, that is both highly simplistic and entirely naive, I wouldn't expect it to be able to display things that are indeterminate like SVGs and the like. Or if they did display them.. only display them as text</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:7vkbgl7un45tvxva25j24yyu/app.bsky.feed.post/3larh4ikppc2n",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:7vkbgl7un45tvxva25j24yyu/app.bsky.feed.post/3largzvg33c2n",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/polyglotprog.bsky.social/post/3larh4ikppc2n",
			"author": {
				"name": "PolyglotProg",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/polyglotprog.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:7vkbgl7un45tvxva25j24yyu/bafkreibzdmdtsygkwyd2wkhrcsyowgfl4igmvoy7cpsdag5aelas44mdwu"
			},
			"date": "2024-11-12T18:20:17.082Z",
			"content": "<p>You have to also remember that using SVGs as stand-in's for rasterized images, is also not how SVGs were intended to be used in the first place.. they are just also really good at doing that as well.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:n5llt2bsouzutg6xf6jg7u34/app.bsky.feed.post/3larh5as2as2x",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:7vkbgl7un45tvxva25j24yyu/app.bsky.feed.post/3largvwekfk2n",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/jeffchausse.bsky.social/post/3larh5as2as2x",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jeff Chausse",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/jeffchausse.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:n5llt2bsouzutg6xf6jg7u34/bafkreifk2b3fp3oppec7jduqdsbafj4ualmxlw4mpddgvfz36txos74ixq"
			},
			"date": "2024-11-12T18:20:42.487Z",
			"content": "<p>Be all that as it may, it’s both something users expect to be able to do, and something Apple certainly could do technically. Semantics are rarely good criteria for making product feature decisions.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:7vkbgl7un45tvxva25j24yyu/app.bsky.feed.post/3larhetj45k2n",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:n5llt2bsouzutg6xf6jg7u34/app.bsky.feed.post/3larh5as2as2x",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/polyglotprog.bsky.social/post/3larhetj45k2n",
			"author": {
				"name": "PolyglotProg",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/polyglotprog.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:7vkbgl7un45tvxva25j24yyu/bafkreibzdmdtsygkwyd2wkhrcsyowgfl4igmvoy7cpsdag5aelas44mdwu"
			},
			"date": "2024-11-12T18:24:56.999Z",
			"content": "<p>LOL... thats Apple's bag baby!... Yes it is entirely possible to do.. but I don't see it happening if I am honest. Most of us that work with SVGs generally do so from the text.. not from any sort of graphical editor.. especially given the fact that most SVGs are dynamically created.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:wjzw74n44kuehrcwoqerbuvn/app.bsky.feed.post/3larmpjz3r22m",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/heydonworks.com/post/3larmpjz3r22m",
			"author": {
